        "id": "ex-qftmath-x01",
        "kind": "example",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Worked example B01 — exact finite dynamics and its first coefficient",
        "statement": "Use the two-level matrix model of [[thm-qft-example-finite-dyson-unitarity]] with $H=g_E\\sigma_x$, where $g_E>0$ is in joules. At\n$$t_1=\\frac{\\pi\\hbar}{2g_E}>0,$$\nthe exact off-diagonal matrix-element square is $1$, while its first-order squared coefficient is $\\pi^2/4>1$. At $t_2=\\pi\\hbar/g_E$, the exact survival matrix-element square is $1$, whereas $e^{-\\Gamma t_2}<1$ for every positive rate $\\Gamma$ in $\\mathrm{s}^{-1}$. These are finite-matrix identities. This mathematical example assigns no probabilistic interpretation to the amplitudes or their matrix-element squares.",
        "deps": [
          "def-countable-choice",
          "def-qft-example-data",
          "thm-qft-example-finite-dyson-unitarity"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
