      {
        "id": "ex-qftmath-x03",
        "kind": "example",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Worked example B03 — nonretarded one-mode correlator",
        "statement": "For the one-mode oscillator in [[lem-qft-example-oscillator-feynman-prescription]], choose $t_*=-\\pi/(2\\omega)$, where $\\omega>0$ is in $\\mathrm{s}^{-1}$. Then the normalized Feynman correlator is $-i/(2\\omega)$, while the explicitly defined kernel $G_R$ is zero. This compares the two functions in the stated one-mode model and makes no claim about a response to an external source.",
